# Citation metadata for nmrForge.
#
# STATUS: usable for citing the repository itself. The author and the repository URL are
# confirmed; the affiliation is not, and no DOI exists yet, so cite the repository URL (every
# release is also citable through its GitHub Release page and tag).
#
# DOI: none, and none reserved. `.zenodo.json` is prepared but still carries an explicit
# placeholder marker - nothing has been uploaded to Zenodo. When a Zenodo release mints a DOI,
# make exactly two changes here: add
#   doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
# and, only if a software paper exists, a `preferred-citation` block; then update the "Citation"
# section of README.md. Never fill in a DOI before the record exists.
#
# `version` and `date-released` are bumped together with core.__version__ on every release;
# tests/test_release_readiness.py fails if the version drifts.
#
# The licence below must not be changed without updating LICENSE, NOTICE, pyproject.toml,
# README.md and LICENSE_OPTIONS.md together (a test enforces that they agree).

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use nmrForge, please cite this metadata (repository URL until a DOI exists)."
title: "nmrForge: automation, parameter optimisation and quality control for Bruker multidimensional NMR data"
abstract: >-
  nmrForge is a platform for automating Bruker multidimensional NMR data processing. It reads
  Bruker acquisition parameters, identifies the experiment type and the sampling scheme, plans a
  processing strategy, drives NMRPipe (and SMILE for non-uniform sampling reconstruction) to
  execute it, performs quality control on the result, and records the resolved parameters,
  external tool versions and warnings so that a run can be reproduced and audited.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Xuanfeng"
    # affiliation: add when confirmed (institute / laboratory)
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RociferX/nmrforge"
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - NMR
  - NMRPipe
  - Bruker
  - non-uniform sampling
  - NUS
  - SMILE
  - spectrum processing
  - quality control
  - reproducibility
  - scientific software
